{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018974-are-there-any-mage-spells-in-1e-that-could-help-a-promethean-with-their-disquiet","id":1018974,"title":"Are there any Mage spells in 1e that could help a Promethean with their Disquiet?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-18T17:23:50-08:00","id":1018974,"title":"Are there any Mage spells in 1e that could help a Promethean with their Disquiet?","content":"As the topic says. In particular, I was hoping their was a spell that could be put in an Imbued Item and given to a Promethean to at least lessen how strong their Disquiet is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T19:04:30-08:00","id":1018993,"title":"","content":"There isn't a written spell that does anything like that, you'd have to make it up. Even then it won't lessen the Disquiet itself, at best it will just mitigate some of the effects. Prometheans are nearly impenetrable to Awakened magic, the degree to which they or anything related to them can be affected by the Supernal can be gathered by reading Tome of the Mysteries, but it's pretty vague and mostly says you can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T19:22:57-08:00","id":1019001,"title":"","content":"hmm, what page, of Tome of Mysteries?<br /> Maybe a spell that granted everyone a certain radius a bonus to rolls made to resist Disquiet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T19:27:01-08:00","id":1019002,"title":"","content":"Hella hard to even know where to begin. The symptoms of Disquiet are most reasonably Mind and Life based, but you couldn't actually chop down the buildup of Disquiet because the problem of Disquiet is the continual presence of a unmitigated force that, when left undirected, manifests as entropy on just every level. Affecting that entropy with Death <i>might</i> get you closer, but even then that's not really the whole of it.<br /> <br /> Disquiet is a result of the Divine Fire, and the problem with this entire conversation is that the Divine Fire is essentially pure <i>change</i>. Trying to cage it or it's effects is like, well, like trying to catch lightning in a bottle.<br /> <br /> By and large I'd just leave it to the Archmasters, but that's me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T22:19:39-08:00","id":1019066,"title":"","content":"Well I guess I should've been more clear that I was speaking of treating the symptoms than the &quot;disease&quot;, so to speak. I.e. slow down how quickly people are made uneasy by Disquiet, even if that means just bolstering their willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T22:49:45-08:00","id":1019079,"title":"","content":"The primary method from which Disquiet seems to kick in is social interaction with a Promethean.<br /> <br /> So you could go blatant with a ring of invisibility, but a more subtle ring of avoidance might work, something that curbs the Promethean's desire to talk to people or just makes people uninterested in talking to them. Vampire has something ideal in Obfuscate, you're just not noticed.<br /> <br /> After Disquiet has been initiated, I think you would need something specific depending on the Promethean and whatever Disquiet they trigger, though I think in most cases you would need a sort of dulling of emotions. Otherwise some sort of item that initiated a mind blank on others after talking with the Promethean might work as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T23:17:11-08:00","id":1019097,"title":"","content":"We have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages\">2E topic talking about those ideas</a> - but it's based on 1E informations, so maybe you can found inspiration in it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T21:04:26-08:00","id":1019595,"title":"","content":"In 1e, there weren't any spells listed to apply to a Promethean in order to mitigate its Disquiet. But there was a shielding spell that could protect a mage from Disquiet; and with an extra dot, that could be extended to others. As well, it was revealed that one of the spells in the Mage core book could be used to purge Disquiet (along with the memories of the Promethean that triggered the Disquiet in the first place).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-20-2016, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T16:52:48-08:00","id":1024000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018974-are-there-any-mage-spells-in-1e-that-could-help-a-promethean-with-their-disquiet?p=1019595#post1019595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, there weren't any spells listed to apply to a Promethean in order to mitigate its Disquiet. But there was a shielding spell that could protect a mage from Disquiet; and with an extra dot, that could be extended to others. As well, it was revealed that one of the spells in the Mage core book could be used to purge Disquiet (along with the memories of the Promethean that triggered the Disquiet in the first place).</div> </div> </div> </div>What spells were those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T16:56:15-08:00","id":1024001,"title":"","content":"My guess for the one that purges Disquiet would be Breach the Vault of Memory, Mind 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}